-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Attribution clause of CC BY-NC 4.0 §3(a) is hereby bound to the
NOTICE file at the root of this repository. Any redistribution,
adaptation, derivative work, or commercially-evaluated copy of this
software must:

  (i)   reproduce this LICENSE file verbatim alongside the work, and

  (ii)  reproduce the NOTICE file verbatim alongside this LICENSE,
        without removing or modifying the citation block, the author
        block, or the attribution paragraph it carries, and

  (iii) cite the SeVim paper using the BibTeX entry given in NOTICE
        (or the venue-specific entry that supersedes it once the
        paper is formally accepted at a journal).

The citation requirement carried by NOTICE persists across any future
relicensing of this software. If this license is later relaxed
(for example, to the MIT or Apache-2.0 license upon formal journal
acceptance), the successor license text must explicitly preserve the
attribution requirement above for any copy that continues to ship the
NOTICE file. A relicensing that drops NOTICE without an equivalent
clause is a breach of the original license terms in the same way that
removing the LICENSE file itself would be.
